course: dictionary
lesson: 13409
title: Hexagonal shapes
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Hexagonal is a long word, but you can break it up. Hexa means six, and the rest tells you it is a shape with corners, like a polygon. So hexagonal means six-sided and six-cornered. «The bees built their honeycomb from hexagonal cells.»
explain: A hexagon has six straight sides and six corners. If a shape is hexagonal, it looks like a hexagon. Try the check: swap in your meaning. «The tiles were hexagonal, with six straight sides each.» Does it still make sense? Yes, so you have it.
explain: Hexagonal words can be tricky. A square has four sides and an octagon has eight, so a hexagonal shape must have six. Count the sides and corners, and you will know the shape.
fact: Hexagonal means shaped like a hexagon: six straight sides and six corners.
fact: Hexagons fit together with no gaps, which is called tessellation.
fact: Honeycomb cells in a beehive are hexagonal.
fact: Snowflakes often have hexagonal, six-fold shapes.
fact: Many nuts for bolts and some pencils are hexagonal, and the Giant's Causeway in Northern Ireland has hexagonal stone columns.
exercise: «The tiles on the kitchen floor were hexagonal.» What does hexagonal mean? | *Shaped with six straight sides and six corners | Round like a circle | Shaped like a star with many points | Shaped with four equal sides
exercise: «The bees filled each hexagonal cell with honey.» How many sides does each cell have? | Four | Eight | *Six | Five
exercise: Mia says a hexagonal pencil has eight sides. Is she right? | *No, hexa means six, so a hexagonal pencil has six sides | Yes, because all pencils have eight sides | No, because pencils are not shapes | Yes, because hexa means eight
test: «The snowflake had a hexagonal pattern.» What does hexagonal mean here? | *Shaped with six sides and six corners | Shaped like a long line | Soft and fluffy | Very cold and icy
test: Which word means the same kind of shape as a honeycomb cell? | Rectangular | *Hexagonal | Triangular | Circular
exam: Which of these shapes has six straight sides and six corners? | Octagon | Triangle | Square | *Hexagon
